    "title": "Community Spotlight: Monticello's Holiday GLOW - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Taylor Mitchell Molly Sweeney ,\n4 hours ago\nMONTICELLO, Ill. (WCIA) — Organizers from the Holiday GLOW in Monticello joined WCIA 3’s Taylor Mitchell in the studio to share more information about the beloved holiday tradition.\nEach year, the University of Illinois Community Credit Union and Allerton Park team up to create a one-mile walk through Allerton.\nCommunity Spotlight: Danville’s Night of Lights parade Derek Peterson, with Allerton Park and Retreat, said they started putting the lights up in October but the planning started months ago.\n“It’s a great family event,” Peterson added.\nLisa Paul, with the University of Illinois Community Credit Union, said she and her family make sure to attend every single year.\n“I told Derek, ‘I want to create a holiday tradition’ and that’s exactly what his team did,” Paul said. “The amount of lights that they’re able to put up in the park is incredible.”\nThe Holiday Glow will be open from 5-9 p.m. from Dec. 5-6, 7-23 and 26-31. Opening weekend will cost $10 per person. After that, it’ll cost $10 per vehicle.\nYou can learn more about the event here .\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WCIA.com.",
